data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrocfw — final report\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## What happened\\n- Dispatched the full requirement to `dev` in d002.\\n- `dev` implemented `src/greet.py` (`greet(name)` returns\\n  `\\\"Hello, {}!\\\".format(name)`) and `tests/test_greet.py` (two tests:\\n  `test_normal_name`, `test_empty_string`), committed as `8d832fa` on\\n  `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`.\\n- Verified independently (not just trusting dev's report): fetched\\n  `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject`, diffed it against base\\n  (`1053761f6a654e7ea58deb67a671a00d2e7fc8ac`) — only the two expected files\\n  added — extracted the tree into a scratch directory, and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself. Result: `OK`, exit 0.\\n- Accepted d002.\\n\\n## Verdict\\nAll three stated criteria are met. Outcome: campaign-met.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

